From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:34:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: let the all-core ceiling be set at
 run time

With every CPU of a cluster busy, clpc caps the cluster at the SoC
table's all-core frequency, which the J604 table sets to what macOS
delivers there: P 3936 / E 2808 MHz. macOS reaches that state another
way: it asks P 4416 / E 2892 MHz and the cluster hardware clocks it
down, so the two may not run at the same voltage.

Add all_core_override, one frequency per cluster type, each applied to
the cluster whose table has it, so the macOS request can be compared
with the table's on the same kernel. The default, 0, keeps the table's
ceilings.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
index 4f8f3dc36f..9a73e18633 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
@@ -272,6 +272,18 @@ static unsigned int apple_clpc_sustain(const struct apple_clpc_hw *hw)
  */
 static bool floor_stock;
 module_param(floor_stock, bool, 0644);
+
+/*
+ * all_core_override: the all-core ceilings to use instead of hw->all_core_khz, one per
+ * cluster type, each matched to the cluster whose table has it (0 = the table's). macOS
+ * asks P 4416000 / E 2892000 with every core busy and the cluster hardware clocks it at
+ * 3936 / 2808 MHz; the table asks 3936000 / 2808000 directly. Default: the table's.
+ */
+static unsigned int all_core_override[2];
+static int all_core_override_count;
+module_param_array(all_core_override, uint, &all_core_override_count, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(all_core_override,
+		 "kHz per cluster type for the all-core ceiling instead of the SoC table (e.g. 4416000,2892000 = what macOS asks; 0 = table)");
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(floor_stock,
 		 "Use the SoC table's CPU floor map and quarters instead of the machine's measured ones (J604: back to DCS 5 / fabric 3 for any busy cluster)");
 
@@ -1096,6 +1108,12 @@ static unsigned int apple_clpc_all_core_khz(struct apple_clpc *clpc,
 
 	if (cl->online < 2 || cl->nbusy < cl->online)
 		return 0;
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(all_core_override); i++) {
+		unsigned int khz = READ_ONCE(all_core_override[i]);
+
+		if (khz && apple_clpc_has_khz(policy, khz))
+			return khz;
+	}
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(clpc->hw->all_core_khz); i++)
 		if (clpc->hw->all_core_khz[i] &&
 		    apple_clpc_has_khz(policy, clpc->hw->all_core_khz[i]))
-- 
2.43.0

